1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,650
Poland has 38 million people today.

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:09,300
On the United Nations' central projection, it shrinks decade after decade.

3
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,725
By 2100: about 19 million. Half.

4
00:00:14,125 --> 00:00:19,296
Very low birth rates, about 1.3 children per woman. Few immigrants.

5
00:00:19,296 --> 00:00:22,075
And many young Poles working abroad.

6
00:00:22,475 --> 00:00:26,433
A big challenge for one of Europe's fastest-growing economies.

7
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:30,775
Where it sits among Europe's biggest populations, in our full video.
